IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `tas-nouns`

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1931 (Tasmania), ss 38A to 40A: publication of proclamations, orders-in-council and prescribed instruments; judicial notice; conditions precedent; changes of names.
-- Answers of a rule of reading: JUST TRUE where the text applies to the case; JUST FALSE only where the text itself says no to the case in its own words
--   (a "means" definition, a condition introduced with "if", "only if", "as long as" or "unless", a list closed with "only", a flat negative, a "where" that fails, a period the text fixes and the case falls outside it);
-- NOTHING everywhere else (an open list, "includes", a term left undefined, silence, a pointer outside the sources, a grant or prohibition limited by its own wording where the case falls outside the limit, a scope limit with no "only").
-- A rule that returns a day, a name or a value has no second not-covered answer, so it returns NOTHING when its text does not apply.
-- The days on which these instruments take effect, s 38A(2)(c) and (d), are in tas-interpretation-time.l4.

§ `s 38A: publication of proclamations, orders-in-council and other instruments`

-- src:751 | (1) Except as provided in subsection (3), the provisions prescribed in subsection (2) apply in respect of –
-- src:753 | (a) every proclamation or order-in-council made in the exercise of a prerogative right of the Crown;
-- src:755 | (b) every proclamation or order-in-council made under an Act or Imperial Act; and
-- src:757 | (c) every prescribed instrument made under an Act.
-- src:787 | (3) The provisions prescribed in subsection (2) do not apply in respect of any proclamation or order-in-council made under an Act or Imperial Act or in respect of a prescribed instrument made under an Act where that Act or Imperial Act expressly provides otherwise.
@ref s 38A(1) and (3) (src:751-757) (src:787)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of instrument`
      `it is made in the exercise of a prerogative right of the Crown` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made under an Act or Imperial Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that Act or Imperial Act expressly provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 38A(1): the provisions prescribed in subsection (2) apply in respect of the instrument` kind `it is made in the exercise of a prerogative right of the Crown` `it is made under an Act or Imperial Act` `that Act or Imperial Act expressly provides otherwise` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (kind EQUALS `a proclamation` OR kind EQUALS `an order-in-council`) AND `it is made in the exercise of a prerogative right of the Crown` THEN JUST TRUE
           IF (kind EQUALS `a proclamation` OR kind EQUALS `an order-in-council` OR kind EQUALS `a prescribed instrument`) AND `it is made under an Act or Imperial Act`
           THEN IF `that Act or Imperial Act expressly provides otherwise` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- A statutory rule that is exempted from the Rules Publication Act 1953 is taken under paragraph (a) (publication), because paragraph (a) names exempted instruments and paragraph (b) names statutory rules without exception (a fork, see NOTES.md).
-- src:761 | (a) if the proclamation, order-in-council, or prescribed instrument is not a statutory rule within the meaning of the Rules Publication Act 1953 or is exempted from the operation of that Act, the proclamation, order-in-council, or prescribed instrument shall be published in the Gazette;
-- src:763 | (b) if the proclamation, order-in-council, or prescribed instrument is a statutory rule within that meaning, the making of the proclamation, order-in-council, or prescribed instrument shall be notified in the Gazette;
@ref s 38A(2)(a) and (b) (src:761-763)
GIVEN `it is a statutory rule within the meaning of the Rules Publication Act 1953` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is exempted from the operation of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Step to be taken in the Gazette`
`s 38A(2)(a) and (b): the step to be taken in the Gazette` `it is a statutory rule within the meaning of the Rules Publication Act 1953` `it is exempted from the operation of that Act` MEANS
    IF `it is a statutory rule within the meaning of the Rules Publication Act 1953` AND NOT (`it is exempted from the operation of that Act`)
    THEN `notification in the Gazette of the making`
    ELSE `publication in the Gazette`

-- src:791 | prescribed instrument means an instrument of a legislative character, other than any proclamation or order-in-council referred to in subsection (1) or a regulation.
@ref s 38A(4) (src:791)
GIVEN `for the purposes of section 38A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an instrument of a legislative character` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a proclamation or order-in-council referred to in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 38A(4): the instrument is a prescribed instrument` `for the purposes of section 38A` `it is an instrument of a legislative character` `it is a proclamation or order-in-council referred to in subsection (1)` `it is a regulation` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`for the purposes of section 38A`) THEN NOTHING
           IF `it is an instrument of a legislative character` AND (NOT (`it is a proclamation or order-in-council referred to in subsection (1)`)) AND (NOT (`it is a regulation`)) THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

#ASSERT `s 38A(1): the provisions prescribed in subsection (2) apply in respect of the instrument` `a proclamation` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 38A(1): the provisions prescribed in subsection (2) apply in respect of the instrument` `an order-in-council` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 38A(1): the provisions prescribed in subsection (2) apply in respect of the instrument` `a proclamation` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 38A(1): the provisions prescribed in subsection (2) apply in respect of the instrument` `an order-in-council` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 38A(1): the provisions prescribed in subsection (2) apply in respect of the instrument` `a prescribed instrument` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 38A(1): the provisions prescribed in subsection (2) apply in respect of the instrument` `a proclamation` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 38A(1): the provisions prescribed in subsection (2) apply in respect of the instrument` `a prescribed instrument` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 38A(1): the provisions prescribed in subsection (2) apply in respect of the instrument` `a proclamation` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 38A(1): the provisions prescribed in subsection (2) apply in respect of the instrument` `a prescribed instrument` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 38A(1): the provisions prescribed in subsection (2) apply in respect of the instrument` `a regulation` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 38A(1): the provisions prescribed in subsection (2) apply in respect of the instrument` `a proclamation` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 38A(2)(a) and (b): the step to be taken in the Gazette` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `publication in the Gazette`
#ASSERT `s 38A(2)(a) and (b): the step to be taken in the Gazette` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `publication in the Gazette`
#ASSERT `s 38A(2)(a) and (b): the step to be taken in the Gazette` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `publication in the Gazette`
#ASSERT `s 38A(2)(a) and (b): the step to be taken in the Gazette` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `notification in the Gazette of the making`
#ASSERT `s 38A(4): the instrument is a prescribed instrument` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 38A(4): the instrument is a prescribed instrument` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 38A(4): the instrument is a prescribed instrument` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 38A(4): the instrument is a prescribed instrument` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 38A(4): the instrument is a prescribed instrument` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `ss 39, 39A and 39B: judicial notice`

-- src:793 | 39. Proclamations, &c., to be judicially noticed
-- src:795 | Judicial notice shall be taken of every proclamation and order-in-council by the Governor made or purporting to be made in pursuance of any Act or Imperial Act and published in the Gazette.
@ref s 39 (src:793-795)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of instrument`
      `it is made by the Governor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made or purports to be made in pursuance of an Act or Imperial Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 39: judicial notice shall be taken of the instrument` kind `it is made by the Governor` `it is made or purports to be made in pursuance of an Act or Imperial Act` `it is published in the Gazette` MEANS
    IF (kind EQUALS `a proclamation` OR kind EQUALS `an order-in-council`) AND `it is made by the Governor` AND `it is made or purports to be made in pursuance of an Act or Imperial Act` AND `it is published in the Gazette`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:799 | (1) Subject to subsection (2), judicial notice shall be taken of regulations made or purporting to be made under an Act –
-- src:801 | (a) that are published in the Gazette, in the case of regulations that are not statutory rules within the meaning of the Rules Publication Act 1953; or
-- src:803 | (b) the making of which is notified in the Gazette, in the case of regulations that are statutory rules within that meaning.
@ref s 39A(1) (src:799-803)
GIVEN `the regulations are made or purport to be made under an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are statutory rules within the meaning of the Rules Publication Act 1953` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the making of them is notified in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 39A(1): judicial notice shall be taken of the regulations` `the regulations are made or purport to be made under an Act` `they are statutory rules within the meaning of the Rules Publication Act 1953` `they are published in the Gazette` `the making of them is notified in the Gazette` MEANS
    IF `the regulations are made or purport to be made under an Act`
       AND (IF `they are statutory rules within the meaning of the Rules Publication Act 1953` THEN `the making of them is notified in the Gazette` ELSE `they are published in the Gazette`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:805 | (2) Notwithstanding subsection (1), a court, judge, or justice may require proof of the making of any regulations referred to in that subsection or of their publication in the Gazette, or, as the case may be, of the notification in the Gazette of their making.
@ref s 39A(2) (src:805)
GIVEN `the regulations are ones referred to in section 39A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 39A(2): a court, judge or justice may require proof of the making of the regulations or of their publication or notification in the Gazette` `the regulations are ones referred to in section 39A(1)` MEANS
    IF `the regulations are ones referred to in section 39A(1)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- Once proof has been required the text does not say what follows if it is not given, so the answer is NOTHING until proof is given.
GIVEN `section 39A(1) gives judicial notice of the regulations` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a court, judge or justice has required proof` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proof has been given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 39A: judicial notice is taken of the regulations without proof` `section 39A(1) gives judicial notice of the regulations` `a court, judge or justice has required proof` `the proof has been given` MEANS
    CONSIDER `section 39A(1) gives judicial notice of the regulations`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST notice THEN IF `a court, judge or justice has required proof` THEN (IF `the proof has been given` THEN JUST notice ELSE NOTHING) ELSE JUST notice

-- src:809 | (1) Subject to subsection (2), judicial notice is to be taken of any order made under an Act by a Minister –
-- src:811 | (a) that is published in the Gazette, in the case of an order that is not a statutory rule within the meaning of the Rules Publication Act 1953; or
-- src:813 | (b) the making of which is notified in the Gazette, in the case of an order that is a statutory rule within the meaning of that Act.
@ref s 39B(1) (src:809-813)
GIVEN `the order is made under an Act by a Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a statutory rule within the meaning of the Rules Publication Act 1953` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the making of it is notified in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 39B(1): judicial notice is to be taken of the order` `the order is made under an Act by a Minister` `it is a statutory rule within the meaning of the Rules Publication Act 1953` `it is published in the Gazette` `the making of it is notified in the Gazette` MEANS
    IF `the order is made under an Act by a Minister`
       AND (IF `it is a statutory rule within the meaning of the Rules Publication Act 1953` THEN `the making of it is notified in the Gazette` ELSE `it is published in the Gazette`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:815 | (2) A court, judge or justice may require proof of –
-- src:817 | (a) the making of an order; or
-- src:819 | (b) the publication of an order in the Gazette; or
-- src:821 | (c) the notification in the Gazette of the making of an order.
@ref s 39B(2) (src:815-821)
GIVEN `the order is one referred to in section 39B(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 39B(2): a court, judge or justice may require proof of the making of the order, of its publication in the Gazette or of the notification in the Gazette of its making` `the order is one referred to in section 39B(1)` MEANS
    IF `the order is one referred to in section 39B(1)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 39: judicial notice shall be taken of the instrument` `a proclamation` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 39: judicial notice shall be taken of the instrument` `an order-in-council` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 39: judicial notice shall be taken of the instrument` `a regulation` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 39: judicial notice shall be taken of the instrument` `a proclamation` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 39: judicial notice shall be taken of the instrument` `a proclamation` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 39: judicial notice shall be taken of the instrument` `a proclamation` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 39A(1): judicial notice shall be taken of the regulations` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 39A(1): judicial notice shall be taken of the regulations` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 39A(1): judicial notice shall be taken of the regulations` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 39A(1): judicial notice shall be taken of the regulations` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 39A(1): judicial notice shall be taken of the regulations` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 39A(2): a court, judge or justice may require proof of the making of the regulations or of their publication or notification in the Gazette` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 39A(2): a court, judge or justice may require proof of the making of the regulations or of their publication or notification in the Gazette` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 39A: judicial notice is taken of the regulations without proof` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 39A: judicial notice is taken of the regulations without proof` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 39A: judicial notice is taken of the regulations without proof` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 39A: judicial notice is taken of the regulations without proof` NOTHING FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 39B(1): judicial notice is to be taken of the order` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 39B(1): judicial notice is to be taken of the order` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 39B(1): judicial notice is to be taken of the order` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 39B(1): judicial notice is to be taken of the order` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 39B(1): judicial notice is to be taken of the order` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 39B(2): a court, judge or justice may require proof of the making of the order, of its publication in the Gazette or of the notification in the Gazette of its making` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 39B(2): a court, judge or justice may require proof of the making of the order, of its publication in the Gazette or of the notification in the Gazette of its making` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 40: conditions precedent need not be recited`

-- src:827 | statutory authority means an incorporated or unincorporated body which is established, constituted or continued by or under an Act or under the royal prerogative, being a body which, or of which the governing authority, wholly or partly comprises a person or persons appointed by the Governor, a Minister of the Crown or another statutory authority.
@ref s 40(1) (src:827)
GIVEN `for the purposes of section 40` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an incorporated or unincorporated body established, constituted or continued by or under an Act or under the royal prerogative` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body, or its governing authority, wholly or partly comprises a person or persons appointed by the Governor, a Minister of the Crown or another statutory authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 40(1): the body is a statutory authority` `for the purposes of section 40` `it is an incorporated or unincorporated body established, constituted or continued by or under an Act or under the royal prerogative` `the body, or its governing authority, wholly or partly comprises a person or persons appointed by the Governor, a Minister of the Crown or another statutory authority` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`for the purposes of section 40`) THEN NOTHING
           IF `it is an incorporated or unincorporated body established, constituted or continued by or under an Act or under the royal prerogative` AND `the body, or its governing authority, wholly or partly comprises a person or persons appointed by the Governor, a Minister of the Crown or another statutory authority` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

DECLARE `Person empowered to make or issue an instrument` IS ONE OF
    `the Governor`
    `a Minister`
    `a statutory authority`
    `a rule-making authority`
    `a specified officer`
    `any other person`

-- src:829 | (2) If by any Act the Governor, a Minister, a statutory authority, a rule-making authority or any specified officer is empowered to make or issue any proclamation, order-in-council, order, warrant or other instrument, it is sufficient to cite in the proclamation, order-in-council, order, warrant or instrument the Act authorising its making or issuing, and it is not necessary to recite or set forth any facts or circumstances or the performance of any conditions precedent upon which that power depends or may be exercised.
@ref s 40(2) sufficient to cite (src:829)
GIVEN `by an Act the person is empowered to make or issue a proclamation, order-in-council, order, warrant or other instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `Person empowered to make or issue an instrument`
      `the Act authorising its making or issuing is cited in the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 40(2): the citation is sufficient` `by an Act the person is empowered to make or issue a proclamation, order-in-council, order, warrant or other instrument` person `the Act authorising its making or issuing is cited in the instrument` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT (`by an Act the person is empowered to make or issue a proclamation, order-in-council, order, warrant or other instrument`)) OR person EQUALS `any other person` THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "If": the persons are named inside the "If" clause
           IF `the Act authorising its making or issuing is cited in the instrument` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- a grant limited by its own wording

-- src:829 | (2) If by any Act the Governor, a Minister, a statutory authority, a rule-making authority or any specified officer is empowered to make or issue any proclamation, order-in-council, order, warrant or other instrument, it is sufficient to cite in the proclamation, order-in-council, order, warrant or instrument the Act authorising its making or issuing, and it is not necessary to recite or set forth any facts or circumstances or the performance of any conditions precedent upon which that power depends or may be exercised.
@ref s 40(2) not necessary to recite (src:829)
GIVEN `by an Act the person is empowered to make or issue a proclamation, order-in-council, order, warrant or other instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `Person empowered to make or issue an instrument`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 40(2): it is not necessary to recite or set forth the facts, circumstances or conditions precedent` `by an Act the person is empowered to make or issue a proclamation, order-in-council, order, warrant or other instrument` person MEANS
    IF (NOT (`by an Act the person is empowered to make or issue a proclamation, order-in-council, order, warrant or other instrument`)) OR person EQUALS `any other person`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "If"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `s 40(1): the body is a statutory authority` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 40(1): the body is a statutory authority` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 40(1): the body is a statutory authority` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 40(1): the body is a statutory authority` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 40(2): the citation is sufficient` TRUE `the Governor` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 40(2): the citation is sufficient` TRUE `a Minister` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 40(2): the citation is sufficient` TRUE `a statutory authority` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 40(2): the citation is sufficient` TRUE `a rule-making authority` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 40(2): the citation is sufficient` TRUE `a specified officer` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 40(2): the citation is sufficient` TRUE `any other person` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 40(2): the citation is sufficient` TRUE `the Governor` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 40(2): the citation is sufficient` FALSE `the Governor` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 40(2): it is not necessary to recite or set forth the facts, circumstances or conditions precedent` TRUE `the Governor` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 40(2): it is not necessary to recite or set forth the facts, circumstances or conditions precedent` TRUE `a specified officer` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 40(2): it is not necessary to recite or set forth the facts, circumstances or conditions precedent` TRUE `any other person` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 40(2): it is not necessary to recite or set forth the facts, circumstances or conditions precedent` FALSE `a Minister` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 40A: changes in names of bodies and offices`

DECLARE `Change of name` HAS
    `the former name` IS A STRING
    `the changed name` IS A STRING

-- src:831 | 40A. Changes in names of bodies and offices
-- src:833 | If a body referred to in an Act changes its name, a reference in the Act to the former name of the body is to be read as a reference to the changed name of the body.
@ref s 40A (src:831-833)
GIVEN `a body referred to in an Act changes its name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reference in the Act is to the former name of the body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 40A: the reference is to be read as a reference to the changed name of the body` `a body referred to in an Act changes its name` `the reference in the Act is to the former name of the body` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`a body referred to in an Act changes its name`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "If"
           IF NOT (`the reference in the Act is to the former name of the body`) THEN NOTHING   -- a scope limit with no "only"
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

GIVEN changes IS A LIST OF `Change of name`
      reference IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 40A: the name that a reference to the name is to be read as a reference to` changes reference MEANS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN c YIELD c's `the former name` EQUALS reference) changes
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN c FOLLOWED BY rest THEN JUST (c's `the changed name`)

#ASSERT `s 40A: the reference is to be read as a reference to the changed name of the body` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 40A: the reference is to be read as a reference to the changed name of the body` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 40A: the reference is to be read as a reference to the changed name of the body` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 40A: the name that a reference to the name is to be read as a reference to` (LIST `Change of name` OF "the Board of Works", "the Works Authority") "the Board of Works" EQUALS JUST "the Works Authority"
#ASSERT `s 40A: the name that a reference to the name is to be read as a reference to` (LIST `Change of name` OF "the Board of Works", "the Works Authority") "the Works Authority" EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 40A: the name that a reference to the name is to be read as a reference to` (EMPTY) "the Board of Works" EQUALS NOTHING
